Error [jet.ArgumentCountMismatch]: `meta.events` takes `watch: .Functions{marked: m}` or `watch: .Calls{to: f}` and a handler
  --> tests/ui/meta_ladder_events_watch_shape.jet:13:10
    |
 13 |     meta.events(.Functions{marked: Traced{}}, (event) -> {})
    |          ^^^^^^
 Why: The watch names what the handler hears: each checked function that carries a marker of the type of the marker value `m`, or each checked call of the function `f`
 Fix: Write `meta.events(watch: .Functions{marked: Traced{}}, (event) -> { … })` or `meta.events(watch: .Calls{to: print}, (event) -> { … })`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0104

Error [jet.MarkerLookupNotMarker]: `Plain` is not a marker
  --> tests/ui/meta_ladder_events_watch_shape.jet:14:43
    |
 14 |     meta.events(watch: .Functions{marked: Plain{}}, (event) -> {})
    |                                           ^^^^^^^
 Why: `meta.events` watches the functions that carry the marker of the watched value's type, so the value is a marker struct's (one with an `impl Marker` block)
 Fix: Watch a marker struct value visible here, as in `.Functions{marked: Traced{}}`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E1134
